    [Performance][Ops] Skip invisible KPool page-table loads (#18596)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Main-branch counterpart of #18576, carrying the same two-file minimal
    change.
    
    In the int32 paged-cache scoring path, the final tile may contain pools
    that are within configured capacity but beyond the query's actual
    visible prefix. Key loads already use the visibility mask, while
    block-table loads previously used only the capacity mask.
    
    Use the existing `valid = (pools < max_pool_seq_len) & (pools <
    visible)` mask for block-table loads as well. This is the only
    production behavior change: invisible pool lanes no longer perform
    page-table reads. Valid-input scores and selected token indices are
    expected to remain unchanged.
    
    The final diff contains only this mask change and boundary cases added
    to the existing eager/graph regression test. No helper extraction,
    wrapper reorganization, new benchmark/compilation-audit scripts or
    documentation expansion is included.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No API, serving flag, score formula or output-layout change. Dense score
    allocation and `torch.topk` remain capacity-wide. This patch does not
    resolve 1M-capacity scratch/TopK overhead, and no isolated end-to-end
    speedup has been established for this mask-only change.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Local Python syntax, repository-pinned Ruff check/format and
    whitespace checks passed.
    - Full local `bash format.sh ci` was attempted but actionlint
    environment installation failed on this Windows host. Full CI remains
    pending.
    - Extend the existing paged scoring and causal-tail regression with
    capacities 127/128/129 around the 128-pool tile boundary, in both eager
    and graph modes. The existing replay step also shortens visible lengths
    and checks selection, tail and padding against the CPU reference.
    - Target NPU validation remains pending in the requested separate
    environment; previous full-model performance and GSM8K smoke results are
    not validation of this reduced revision.
    
    ```bash
    pytest -q tests/e2e/nightly/single_node/ops/singlecard_ops/triton/test_glm5next_pool_key_indexer_triton.py
    ```
    
    #### Related full-model ITL comparison
    
    For **4K input / 2K output** (4096 / 2048 tokens), the author-reported
    mean ITL improved from approximately **116 ms to 96 ms**, a reduction of
    **20 ms (17.2%)**.
    
    | Input tokens | Output tokens | Mean ITL before | Mean ITL after |
    Reduction |
    | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
    | 4096 | 2048 | ~116 ms | ~96 ms | ~17.2% |
    
    These figures describe the earlier full-model dense-serving
    optimization. They are performance context, not a controlled
    before/after measurement of this PR's reduced page-table mask change;
    target-runtime validation of this revision remains pending.
    
